From 10031e18233c5a4b0f9774d46e65ae82bba7b519 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:23:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(youth): calibrate the actual sandal sole slab instead of
 lowest bind-pose vertices

Root cause of the CI blocker "Original sandal plane is too ambiguous to
flatten R" (LOD 3, runs 45693491554 / 45693492317): the original Meshy
youth is bound with both sandals rolled ~80 deg inward. The lowest
Foot/Toe-weighted vertices are the lateral foot wall, so the previous
lowest-28%-per-segment plane fit was rolled 36-52 deg on LOD 0-2 and
degenerate on LOD 3 (20 right-foot vertices).

- youth_anatomy.sole_patch: largest connected coplanar (12 deg) Foot/Toe
  surface = wooden sandal slab; coplanar fragments merged; gates: area
  >= 40 cm2, dominance over differently oriented flat surfaces >= 1.5,
  max plane residual 4 mm, slab faces away from the ankle, left/right
  mirror <= 12 deg.
- retarget_accad_youth: LOD-family gate (each LOD within 12 deg of
  LOD 0), sole planes written to the report, grounding samples include
  every foot vertex on or beyond the slab plane.
- youth_sole_contact.gd: runtime grounding samples the same slab rule
  from the report; youth_mocap_test checks it per LOD.

Gate change (explicit, not silent): the former rest-normal y >= 0.35
check is replaced. On this asset the true slab normal has y = 0.13-0.25
on every LOD, so that check rejected the correct sole and accepted
mis-fitted walls on LOD 0-2.

Measured (local, Godot 4.7.2 headless + numpy skinning of the produced
GLBs): sole slab tilt in ground contact before 59-76 deg, after idle
1.7-4.7 deg, march mean 11-13 deg; no foot vertex below floor. Open:
more >1.5x stretched leg edges at LOD 0 (idle 2 -> 36, march 39 -> 64
of 12521); visual and Fold7 acceptance still required.

